cjson is header-only.

System install (headers -> /usr/include/cjson, so <cjson/cjson.hpp> resolves):

    sudo scripts/install_local.py

In-tree use: the headers live under src/cjson/; duck's default include path (-i ./src)
makes <cjson/cjson.hpp> resolve from the repo root, or point your compiler at src/.

Requirements: g++ >= 14 (cjson uses -std=c++26 and `if consteval`), the micron core
library (installed at /usr/include/micron or as a sibling ../micron dev tree). No libc,
no STL, no other dependencies.

Tests/benches additionally want: the micron dev tree as a sibling (../micron, for
snowball + bbench), and for the comparison benches: the installed yyjson
(/usr/lib64/libyyjson.so) plus the simdjson reference checkout at ../../Git/simdjson
(scripts/vsbuild amalgamates it on demand into comparison/.simdjson-build/).
